      ⍝ Integer overflow → float promotion (IntCell::bif_multiply_ii()).
      ⍝ Like + and -, × now promotes only on a genuine int64 overflow
      ⍝ (via __builtin_mul_overflow, exact) -- it used to promote as
      ⍝ soon as a double-precision approximation of the product crossed
      ⍝ the conservative LARGE_INT/SMALL_INT threshold (≈9.2E18, ⎕SYL
      ⍝ "largest/smallest integer"), well before the true int64 boundary
      ⍝ (≈9.223E18), losing precision for no reason (Bugs28 #82).
      ⍝ ⎕PP←17 so the still-promoted (genuinely overflowing) results
      ⍝ print with enough digits to be unambiguous.
      ⍝
      ⎕PP←17

      ⍝ below the true int64 limit either way: stays integer
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ 64-bit integers (IBM APL2: 32 bit)
      1000000000×9199999999
9199999999000000000
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2
      26⎕CR 1000000000×9199999999
16
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP

