      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #79): ComplexCell::is_near_real() used to
      ⍝ treat *any* complex number with an absolutely-tiny imaginary
      ⍝ part as real, regardless of how the real part compared -- so a
      ⍝ product of two comparably-tiny complex numbers displayed with
      ⍝ its J part silently dropped, even though the underlying value
      ⍝ was correct (as the third line below shows by scaling it back
      ⍝ into a displayable range).
      ⍝
      1J1×1E¯20J1E¯20
0J2E¯20

